rem Convex Path in Square
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=604

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

arg N integer = 1000000000000000000

rem Steps are primitive vectors (a, b)
rem with distinct slopes, and both
rem sums must stay within N. A layer
rem a + b = s holds phi(s) vectors of
rem cost s and is balanced, so take
rem whole layers while the cost stays
rem within 2 N, then fill with layer
rem m + 1. Exact fills with an odd
rem rest are not special-cased.
L = (((10.0 * N) ** (1.0 / 3.0)) floor)
L = L * 11 // 10 + 100
Ph = (0 to L) copy
for P in primes to L
  Sl = P to L by P
  Ph Sl -= Ph Sl // P
end
Ss = 2 to L
Cs = (Ss * Ph (2 to L)) scan +
Ps = Ph (2 to L) scan +
M = (Cs at most (2 * N)) count
R = 2 * N - Cs (M - 1)
T = R // (M + 2)
Answer = Ps (M - 1) + T + 1
Answer print
